 :constraints
 ["PI_BIN, PI_PROVIDER, and PI_MODEL must be read from environment (PI_BIN defaulting to `pi` on PATH) to construct each subprocess invocation of the pi CLI; no direct LLM API call or API key handling exists anywhere in this codebase — all suggestion/chat generation goes through the pi CLI subprocess"
  "WHISPER_BIN env var must point to a whisper.cpp binary compiled with CUDA support"
  "All audio transcription uses subprocess calls to whisper.cpp; no JNI bindings"
  "Session logs are append-only EDN files in data/sessions/; no SQL or NoSQL database"
  "Server listens on port from PORT env var, defaulting to 7777"
  "All concurrent coordination uses core.async channels; no Thread/sleep"
  "Close http-kit server and all open SSE channels on system stop"
  "Java 21 or higher required"
  "No frontend build step; all assets served via CDN links or resources/public"]

 :anti-goals
 ["No WebRTC; use MediaRecorder HTTP POST for audio delivery"
  "No durable message queue such as Kafka or RabbitMQ; core.async channels only"
  "No React or ClojureScript; HTMX plus server-rendered hiccup2 only"
  "No SQL or NoSQL database; EDN append-only logs only"
  "No Docker in this iteration; bare-metal run instructions only"
  "No authentication or multi-user access control"
  "No streaming from whisper.cpp; batch transcribe per audio chunk"
  "No Tailwind CLI build; Tailwind Play CDN only"
  "http-kit's own client (org.httpkit.client), if used at all, is only for the SSE/HTTP server layer and any tool script's own external calls (e.g. web_search) — never for LLM communication, which goes through the pi CLI subprocess exclusively"
  "No structured function-calling/tool schema of any kind (Anthropic or OpenAI style) passed to an LLM API; tools are plain executable scripts in the pi subprocess's working directory that pi's own bash tool discovers and invokes itself"
  "No multi-step tool_call/tool_result loop implemented in Clojure; pi's own internal agent loop handles calling tool scripts as needed within a single subprocess invocation per turn"
  "No persistent/daemon pi process; every turn is a fresh subprocess, and this latency cost is accepted deliberately in exchange for reusing pi's existing harness"]

